        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nOur inequality contains only \"less than\" symbols. So, the endpoints $-11$ and $-3$ are *not* included. \n\n$$\n-11\\,\\,<\\,\\,x\\,\\,<\\,\\,-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\n(-11,-3)\n$$\n\nMore formally, we can also write\n\n$$\nx\\in (-11,-3).\n$$"
      },
